course: dictionary
lesson: 6073
title: Mesh: a net, a fit, a turn
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mesh is a word with more than one meaning. Most often it is a material made of threads or wires woven together, with small holes between them, like a net. You can see wire mesh in a fence or in a bag for oranges.
explain: Mesh can also be a verb. «Our ideas meshed» means our ideas fitted together well. Gear wheels mesh too, when their teeth lock together so that one turns the other.
explain: Context tells you which meaning to use. «The metal mesh in a microwave door has holes too small for microwaves to pass through» shows that mesh is the material with holes. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A mesh is made of threads or wires woven together, with small holes between them.
fact: Mesh can be a noun (a net-like material) or a verb (to fit together).
fact: «Gears mesh» means the teeth of two gear wheels lock together so one turns the other.
fact: «Two meshing gears turn in opposite directions.»
fact: Useful phrases: wire mesh, mesh fence, mesh bag, mesh well together.
exercise: «The paper is spread on a fast wire mesh to drain.» What is the wire mesh? | A mushy pulp made from wood | A hot roller that squeezes the paper | *A sheet of woven wires with small holes that let water drain through | A roll of dried paper
exercise: «Our ideas meshed well together.» What does meshed mean here? | Were lost in a mesh fence | *Fitted together smoothly | Broke into pieces | Got wet in the rain
exercise: «Two meshing gears turn in opposite directions.» Which way do two meshing gears turn? | Not at all | *Opposite directions | The same direction, always | Backwards and forwards at the same time
test: «Humphry Davy's safety lamp had a metal mesh around the flame.» Why was the mesh there? | To make the lamp look pretty | *To stop the flame lighting explosive gas in the mine | To hold the lamp up on a hook
test: «Three gears that all mesh with one another in a ring cannot turn at all.» What happens to three meshing gears in a ring? | They spin faster and faster | *They cannot turn at all | They all turn the same way, together
exam: «The metal mesh in a microwave door has holes too small for microwaves to pass through but big enough for light.» Why can you see through the door? | The door is always open | *Light passes through the holes, but microwaves cannot | Microwaves turn the holes into light | The mesh is clear glass, so nothing blocks it
